  },\n  {\n    \"day\": 23,\n    \"title\": \"A permission and budget boundary for the assistant\",\n    \"brief\": \"Harden the fictional document assistant with trusted-user fixtures, document filtering, request limits, and explicit exhausted-budget behavior. Add a small threat model and abuse test set. Keep the prototype's limits visible: fixture identity and single-process budgets demonstrate boundaries but are not a deployed authentication or distributed-quota system.\",\n    \"deliverables\": [\n      \"A trust-boundary diagram and protected-resource list.\",\n      \"Permission filtering before context construction.\",\n      \"Explicit request/resource limits and recovery results.\",\n      \"An abuse-test report and a reproducible cost estimate.\"\n    ],\n    \"acceptance\": [\n      \"Trusted authority is separate from user text and model arguments.\",\n      \"Forbidden documents never enter an unauthorized user's context.\",\n      \"Resource limits are enforced outside the model prompt.\",\n      \"Budget exhaustion and policy rejection produce clear outcomes.\",\n      \"The threat model, attack results, and cost assumptions are recorded.\"\n    ],\n    \"starter\": \"lesson-23-starter.zip\",\n    \"filename\": \"policy_gate.py\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": 24,\n    \"title\": \"FastAPI feedback and question service\",\n    \"brief\": \"Build POST /feedback, GET /feedback/{id}, and POST /ask for the fictional assistant. Use validated request models, a documented SQLite file, parameterized queries, and a trusted-identity boundary or explicitly labelled local identity fixtures. Reuse your answer contract and make invalid, missing, and forbidden outcomes clear. Verify the current FastAPI installation command in the linked documentation.\",\n    \"deliverables\": [\n      \"An API contract and runnable FastAPI service with documented setup.\",\n      \"A durable feedback schema and parameterized storage layer.\",\n      \"Request validation and explicitly sc